\[\Lambda\longrightarrow p+\pi^{-},\mathrm{BR}=63.9\%\]

\[\Sigma^{+}\longrightarrow p+\pi^{0},\mathrm{BR}=51.57\%\]

\[\Xi^{-}\longrightarrow\Lambda+\pi^{-},\mathrm{BR}=99.887\%\]

\[\Xi^{0}\longrightarrow\Lambda+\pi^{0},\mathrm{BR}=99.524\%\]

The \(p_{T}\) spectra of \(\Sigma^{+}\) were obtained by multiplying the \(\Lambda\) spectra by a factor of 0.224 (\(\Sigma^{+}/\Lambda\) = 0.224 was estimated from the thermal model). Based on the ART [115] calculation, we assumed the spectra of \(\Xi^{0}\) and \(\Xi^{-}\) are the same and took 30% of the \(\Xi^{0}\) yield into the estimate of uncertainty.

