\[\begin{split}\frac{dN}{m_{T}dm_{T}dy}&\propto m_{\rm T }\int_{-\eta_{\rm max}}^{\eta_{\rm max}}d\eta\cosh(y-\eta)\\ &\times\int_{0}^{R(\eta)}rdrI_{0}\left(\frac{p_{T}\sinh(\rho)}{T }\right)\times\exp\left(\frac{-m_{T}\cosh(y-\eta)\cosh(\rho)}{T}\right)\end{split} \tag{5.3.3}\]

where \(\eta\equiv\tanh^{-1}(z/t)\) is the boost angle, denotes the space-time rapidity. Following the approach analyzed above, we use the same setup in order to break the longitudinal boost-invariance, and in the transverse direction boundary, considering the fireball with two choices, the first one is an elliptic shape of \(R(\eta)\) given by

