where \(\mu\) is the center value and \(\sigma\) is the width of the Gaussian distribution. For a given \(R_{0}\) = 10, \(\mu\) = 0, and \(\sigma\) = 1.045, the shape is shown in Fig. 5.3.3 right panel.

